WEBVTT

1
00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.046
Grandfather.

2
00:02:49.015 --> 00:02:52.886
This is for my family.

3
00:02:52.886 --> 00:02:56.122
An excellent harvest, Tsering.

4
00:02:57.757 --> 00:03:04.798
How long do you think it
will feed us?

5
00:03:04.798 --> 00:03:07.600
A very long time.

6
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.736
A lifetime.

7
00:03:11.137 --> 00:03:18.078
With all this we can't even feed
the village for three months.

8
00:03:18.078 --> 00:03:21.014
Look grandfather, it's the caravan.

9
00:03:21.014 --> 00:03:22.916
The caravan.

10
00:05:03.316 --> 00:05:05.118
Lhakpa.

11
00:05:19.666 --> 00:05:22.702
Tinle, your son has died.

12
00:05:25.772 --> 00:05:28.541
He wanted to take a different route.

13
00:05:28.541 --> 00:05:31.678
He said it was a one-day shortcut.

14
00:05:33.446 --> 00:05:38.785
I told him it was dangerous
but he wouldn't listen.

15
00:05:38.785 --> 00:05:42.455
A couple of hours later I found him. Dead.

16
00:05:45.859 --> 00:05:49.062
This salt has been mixed with sand.

17
00:05:51.264 --> 00:05:54.467
What are you waiting for? Take him off.

18
00:07:32.632 --> 00:07:34.401
Well?

19
00:07:38.038 --> 00:07:41.808
Tsering, I told you...

20
00:07:41.808 --> 00:07:47.447
your father will be reborn
in the kingdom Padmasambhava.

21
00:07:47.447 --> 00:07:48.915
When?

22
00:07:52.952 --> 00:07:56.523
It'll take a while for him to get there.

23
00:07:56.523 --> 00:08:03.296
He must fly over hell before
he reaches Buddha's paradise.

24
00:08:03.296 --> 00:08:06.666
Everyone will have to die in the end.

25
00:08:06.666 --> 00:08:10.270
For how long will we stay dead?

26
00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:13.306
All that lives has to die.

27
00:08:13.306 --> 00:08:16.009
It is reborn again and dies again too.

28
00:08:16.009 --> 00:08:19.779
How many lives does it take to become a leader?

29
00:08:19.779 --> 00:08:23.650
We have been leaders for a very long time.

30
00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:26.019
You will be next.

31
00:08:26.019 --> 00:08:28.655
Will you teach me what to do?

32
00:08:56.149 --> 00:08:57.984
Thank you.

33
00:08:57.984 --> 00:09:00.754
Lhakpa defied the mountains.

34
00:09:00.754 --> 00:09:03.757
The mountains haven't done anything to him.

35
00:09:03.757 --> 00:09:07.927
I know them very well.
- You do, but Lhakpa doesn't.

36
00:09:08.128 --> 00:09:10.864
He is my son.

37
00:09:12.098 --> 00:09:15.035
He has inherited my forces.

38
00:09:16.069 --> 00:09:19.639
Your pride and persistance
is what you mean.

39
00:09:19.639 --> 00:09:23.810
You don't know anything.
Karma lied.

40
00:09:25.912 --> 00:09:30.884
He has caused that accident
because he wants to be the leader.

41
00:09:36.723 --> 00:09:38.992
I know what I'm saying.

42
00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:43.029
Who will bring us the salt now?

43
00:09:43.029 --> 00:09:46.099
And what about the wheat?

44
00:09:46.099 --> 00:09:48.702
Who will be taking care of the Yaks?

45
00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:52.572
No leader, no land.

46
00:09:54.808 --> 00:09:57.377
No woman, no husband.

47
00:09:57.377 --> 00:09:59.446
My son without a father.

48
00:12:56.323 --> 00:12:59.059
This is not our lucky day.

49
00:12:59.059 --> 00:13:01.561
Let's try again.

50
00:13:01.561 --> 00:13:04.197
This time I'll hit the target.

51
00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:15.475
Karma, I have no luck today.
You take the shot.

52
00:13:18.178 --> 00:13:21.114
I will make a wish for you.

53
00:13:51.778 --> 00:13:53.947
The Gods triumph.

54
00:13:59.386 --> 00:14:02.222
Thanks to you my child will live.

55
00:14:02.222 --> 00:14:06.059
You have shattered the heart
of the evil spirit.

56
00:14:06.059 --> 00:14:10.930
The evil spirit has died,
but your daughter isn't safe yet.

57
00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:13.433
Get the doctor over here.

58
00:14:13.433 --> 00:14:16.069
I have more faith in you.

59
00:14:18.738 --> 00:14:21.374
I've been looking everywhere.

60
00:14:21.374 --> 00:14:25.145
Karma's hit the target.

61
00:14:25.145 --> 00:14:28.348
Ask him to teach me how to shoot.

62
00:14:32.652 --> 00:14:35.355
Come on let's go home.

63
00:14:35.355 --> 00:14:41.161
Who will teach me now?
- Don't worry, you're still young.

64
00:14:41.161 --> 00:14:44.831
But I will become the next leader.

65
00:14:44.831 --> 00:14:48.902
With daddy's bow.
- I've thrown it into the river.

66
00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:52.472
Don't cry.

67
00:14:52.472 --> 00:14:55.575
That was a lie. It's in the house.

68
00:14:55.575 --> 00:14:57.877
It's yours now.

69
00:15:03.083 --> 00:15:08.722
Karma was Lhakpa's right hand man.
He is the one that should be leader.

70
00:15:08.722 --> 00:15:12.859
He is experienced.
- He has the strength and knowledge it takes.

71
00:15:13.093 --> 00:15:15.795
I will be leading the caravan.

72
00:15:15.795 --> 00:15:18.598
I've done it a thousand times before.

73
00:15:18.598 --> 00:15:20.433
Lhakpa is dead.

74
00:15:21.434 --> 00:15:26.139
His son Tsering should take over.
He is going alright.

75
00:15:27.407 --> 00:15:30.610
It'll take years
before he makes a good leader.

76
00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:33.213
The gods are on my side.

77
00:15:33.213 --> 00:15:39.085
Tinle, we have faith in you
and in your experience.

78
00:15:39.085 --> 00:15:44.157
But your legs
they're not what they used to be.

79
00:15:44.157 --> 00:15:49.095
I will take a strong man with me.
He will be my support.

80
00:15:49.095 --> 00:15:51.665
Karma would be best.

81
00:15:51.665 --> 00:15:54.067
Karma is a traitor.

82
00:15:54.067 --> 00:15:58.705
He isn't to blame
for the murder of past generations.

83
00:15:58.705 --> 00:16:03.376
They killed my grandfather.
And now they've killed my son.

84
00:16:04.411 --> 00:16:08.581
It was an accident.
Karma didn't do it.

85
00:16:08.682 --> 00:16:10.784
Nonsense.

86
00:16:10.784 --> 00:16:14.955
Kharma was chosen by the Council.
- The Council is me.

87
00:16:17.824 --> 00:16:21.628
You wouldn't be here
if it wasn't for me.

88
00:16:21.628 --> 00:16:26.166
Tinle, there is no time
to find a better man.

89
00:16:50.357 --> 00:16:55.061
Lama, what have you decided?
- The fifteenth constellation.

90
00:16:57.364 --> 00:17:01.534
The Thirteenth day, Monday,
the fifteenth constellation.

91
00:17:01.768 --> 00:17:03.870
Let me have a look.

92
00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.740
The thirteenth day...

93
00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:09.676
well? When do we leave?

94
00:17:11.244 --> 00:17:14.981
Be patient.
- It's always the same.

95
00:17:14.981 --> 00:17:18.985
You are putting our lives at stake
with those calculations of yours.

96
00:17:18.985 --> 00:17:21.688
The twelfth or thirteenth day.

97
00:17:21.688 --> 00:17:23.657
Be patient.

98
00:17:23.657 --> 00:17:29.195
We were doing it this way already
before you were born.

99
00:17:29.195 --> 00:17:34.467
The thirteenth day, the fifteenth
constellation. This is the best day.

100
00:17:34.467 --> 00:17:38.571
Snow storms don't wait.

101
00:17:39.906 --> 00:17:44.844
The fifteenth constellation?
Isn't that later?

102
00:17:44.844 --> 00:17:47.013
That's settled then.

103
00:17:49.082 --> 00:17:50.984
Is it this day?

104
00:17:52.852 --> 00:17:56.623
Monday, the fifteenth constellation...

105
00:18:14.307 --> 00:18:16.876
I can't help you Tinle.

106
00:18:19.346 --> 00:18:22.983
A bag of salt
doesn't change anything.

107
00:18:22.983 --> 00:18:26.553
It would be treachery
if I took your offer.

108
00:18:26.553 --> 00:18:30.256
Go to Karma.
He's the best.

109
00:18:30.256 --> 00:18:33.526
You and your 'Karma'.

110
00:18:33.526 --> 00:18:36.129
Karma this... Karma that.

111
00:18:36.129 --> 00:18:39.532
He will lead you into death.
You're out of your mind.

112
00:18:39.532 --> 00:18:42.268
You're wrong, Tinle.

113
00:18:42.268 --> 00:18:45.538
Karma tried to save Lhakpa.

114
00:18:45.538 --> 00:18:48.008
Karma can drop dead.

115
00:18:48.008 --> 00:18:52.178
He wants to take my place.
You're all trying to set me up.

116
00:19:09.296 --> 00:19:12.999
Doesn't my beer taste good, Rabkie?

117
00:19:12.999 --> 00:19:17.070
It does, just don't let your husband
drink too much.

118
00:19:42.862 --> 00:19:46.533
Tinle, let's call for a truce.

119
00:19:46.533 --> 00:19:50.303
You will need me.
You will not find anyone else.

120
00:19:50.303 --> 00:19:52.806
I don't need you.

121
00:19:52.806 --> 00:19:55.408
Why are you treating me like this?

122
00:19:55.408 --> 00:19:58.511
Lhakpa was my friend.

123
00:19:58.511 --> 00:20:03.383
I forbid you to say his name.
The mountains have seen everything.

124
00:20:03.383 --> 00:20:06.953
I will lead the caravan.

125
00:20:06.953 --> 00:20:09.489
Alone you will.

126
00:20:09.489 --> 00:20:13.627
No one is going with you.
You haven't done this in years.

127
00:20:13.793 --> 00:20:19.032
They will accept me. I was their leader
before you were even born.

128
00:20:19.032 --> 00:20:22.302
Tsering will be my successor
before you die.

129
00:20:22.302 --> 00:20:26.172
Your hate will not
help your sorrow, Tinle.

130
00:20:34.881 --> 00:20:39.686
The Lama's have concluded
on the day of departure.

131
00:20:39.686 --> 00:20:43.657
We lave in ten days.

132
00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:49.763
Grandfather.

133
00:20:49.763 --> 00:20:52.399
Who will take our Yaks?

134
00:20:58.638 --> 00:21:02.609
Grandfather, what is wrong?

135
00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:08.381
Don't worry.
We'll find someone.

136
00:21:08.448 --> 00:21:11.384
There's still ten days left.

137
00:21:51.257 --> 00:21:54.094
Are you ignoring me?

138
00:21:54.094 --> 00:21:57.664
We must obey the gods.

139
00:21:57.664 --> 00:22:01.334
You don't belong in the
mountains anymore.

140
00:22:01.334 --> 00:22:07.674
My son has died in there.
- We can't help you.

141
00:22:07.674 --> 00:22:10.944
Don't force us to say no.

142
00:22:19.586 --> 00:22:22.822
Grandfather.

143
00:22:22.822 --> 00:22:26.026
Why do they refuse to help you?

144
00:22:28.928 --> 00:22:33.400
It's not easy to
take your father's place.

145
00:22:45.412 --> 00:22:49.616
Have you forgotten the way home?

146
00:22:49.616 --> 00:22:52.319
It's been a while indeed.

147
00:22:55.655 --> 00:23:00.994
Every time you want to change your destiny
you come to me.

148
00:23:11.905 --> 00:23:14.341
Come here, boy.

149
00:23:24.017 --> 00:23:28.188
From now on you will be called Pasang.

150
00:23:28.288 --> 00:23:31.091
My name is Tsering.

151
00:23:31.091 --> 00:23:33.360
From now on you're Pasang.

152
00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:36.730
The lama's have called me Tsering.

153
00:23:49.876 --> 00:23:54.714
Evil spirits are on their way.
They're jealous at us.

154
00:23:54.714 --> 00:23:57.484
We have a lot of Yaks.

155
00:23:57.484 --> 00:24:02.389
If we give you a blacksmith's name
they will not harm you.

156
00:24:02.389 --> 00:24:07.360
Your father is dead.
It is your task to replace him.

157
00:24:07.360 --> 00:24:09.663
I will help you.

158
00:25:14.794 --> 00:25:17.030
What are you doing, Karma?

159
00:25:23.136 --> 00:25:25.472
I'm leaving.

160
00:25:25.472 --> 00:25:28.575
Now? You can't leave now.

161
00:25:28.575 --> 00:25:32.045
Winter is coming.

162
00:25:32.045 --> 00:25:37.050
Do you believe in those calculations?
- It is the Gods.

163
00:25:37.050 --> 00:25:40.086
They can say whatever they want.

164
00:25:40.086 --> 00:25:44.224
Are you leaving all by yourself?
- Me and my Yaks.

165
00:25:44.391 --> 00:25:46.226
Join me.

166
00:25:48.295 --> 00:25:51.498
My father would kill me.

167
00:25:51.498 --> 00:25:55.635
Who's carrying the salt? You or your father?

168
00:25:55.635 --> 00:25:59.372
He is too old. We'll join Tinle.

169
00:25:59.372 --> 00:26:00.840
Yeah, Tinle.

170
00:26:04.044 --> 00:26:06.479
Speaking of young men.

171
00:28:17.210 --> 00:28:19.012
Come here.

172
00:28:21.481 --> 00:28:24.117
Take Tinle to Norbou.

173
00:28:32.025 --> 00:28:34.961
Grandfather Tinle, come with me.

174
00:29:14.601 --> 00:29:16.436
Is this color right?

175
00:29:22.976 --> 00:29:27.714
The blue isn't as clear
as it was yesterday. Watch closely.

176
00:29:29.783 --> 00:29:32.285
We'll never finish this in time.

177
00:29:32.285 --> 00:29:38.391
That is up to the Gods. We do not determine
when we're done.

178
00:29:38.391 --> 00:29:41.027
We have no influence on it.

179
00:29:41.027 --> 00:29:46.132
The fresco knows
when it is done.

180
00:30:00.180 --> 00:30:02.248
What is it?

181
00:30:03.817 --> 00:30:05.652
Why are you here?

182
00:30:08.188 --> 00:30:09.623
Norbou...

183
00:30:12.659 --> 00:30:14.494
Father.

184
00:30:19.966 --> 00:30:24.404
Karma, teach me how to use the bow.

185
00:30:24.404 --> 00:30:31.211
First you have to get strong arms.
It's very important. Do you understand?

186
00:30:31.211 --> 00:30:33.179
Come.

187
00:30:38.618 --> 00:30:41.888
We leave tomorrow morning.
Come with me.

188
00:30:41.888 --> 00:30:47.127
But it's Before the set date!
- There will be snowstorms soon.

189
00:30:47.127 --> 00:30:51.931
You want to leave before Tinle don't you?
- Let's go together.

190
00:30:53.466 --> 00:30:57.370
Come on, Tinle can't do this on his own.

191
00:30:57.370 --> 00:31:03.410
I wanted to join forces
but he refused.

192
00:31:03.410 --> 00:31:06.913
You ask him. Where is he?

193
00:31:06.913 --> 00:31:08.748
He's in the monastery.

194
00:31:15.121 --> 00:31:17.624
He's getting Norbou.

195
00:31:17.624 --> 00:31:20.727
Why would he do that?

196
00:31:20.727 --> 00:31:23.897
He doesn't know what he's doing.

197
00:31:23.897 --> 00:31:29.469
He's nothing but grief.
- And what's tormenting you?

198
00:31:44.084 --> 00:31:46.186
It is impossible.

199
00:31:46.186 --> 00:31:50.056
Karma was my brother's best friend.

200
00:31:50.056 --> 00:31:54.494
Yes, but things have changed.

201
00:31:54.494 --> 00:31:59.799
Your brother is dead
and I can't look after the Yaks alone.

202
00:31:59.799 --> 00:32:04.304
Will you lead the caravan?
- I have no other choice.

203
00:32:04.304 --> 00:32:07.440
Why? Choose someone else.

204
00:32:07.440 --> 00:32:11.611
This man is you, my second son.

205
00:32:11.711 --> 00:32:17.884
I don't know anything about the mountains,
the Yaks or the salt.

206
00:32:17.884 --> 00:32:20.654
You'll learn.
- No.

207
00:32:20.654 --> 00:32:26.393
I've been here since I was eight years old.
I can read, know how to pray and paint.

208
00:32:26.393 --> 00:32:28.995
You wanted me to become a lama.

209
00:32:28.995 --> 00:32:32.132
I am no man to lead a caravan.

210
00:32:32.132 --> 00:32:37.470
You have enough clothes and food.
We don't.

211
00:32:37.470 --> 00:32:41.007
You sent me here as a kid.

212
00:32:41.007 --> 00:32:43.877
And now you want to send me off into the mountains.

213
00:32:43.877 --> 00:32:47.280
You are afraid.
- Not afraid enough to refuse.

214
00:32:47.280 --> 00:32:50.283
You are no longer Lhakpa's brother.

215
00:32:50.283 --> 00:32:53.853
Say your prayers
if that is all you can do.

216
00:32:53.853 --> 00:32:58.325
I'll bring Tsering along.
He at least isn't afraid.

217
00:33:18.445 --> 00:33:20.714
Do we leave tomorrow?

218
00:33:20.714 --> 00:33:23.650
Go to sleep. It'll be a long journey.

219
00:33:23.650 --> 00:33:28.588
My wife wants to say goodbye tonight.
- Enjoy it.

220
00:33:45.672 --> 00:33:47.974
Pema.

221
00:33:47.974 --> 00:33:49.843
Are you there?

222
00:34:06.593 --> 00:34:09.162
Do you remember?

223
00:34:09.162 --> 00:34:13.600
Our hideout when we were kids.
- Did you call me just for that?

224
00:34:13.600 --> 00:34:16.670
You can't leave.

225
00:34:16.670 --> 00:34:20.073
Not before Tinle has returned.

226
00:34:20.073 --> 00:34:24.244
Why not?
It is Tinle's law.

227
00:34:24.477 --> 00:34:26.746
No, it's the Dolpo's.

228
00:34:26.746 --> 00:34:28.848
Tinle isn't the Dolpo.

229
00:34:28.848 --> 00:34:33.420
He will take the decisions for himself, you and the others.

230
00:34:35.722 --> 00:34:38.425
Pema.

231
00:34:38.425 --> 00:34:41.328
Go into mourning.

232
00:34:41.328 --> 00:34:43.630
Come with us.

233
00:34:44.898 --> 00:34:47.734
And bring Tsering.

234
00:34:47.734 --> 00:34:50.370
We will add your Yaks to the troop.

235
00:34:50.370 --> 00:34:53.873
What will you do if you can't
sell the salt?

236
00:34:53.873 --> 00:34:55.942
Tinle will return.

237
00:34:55.942 --> 00:34:58.645
Tinle is old.

238
00:34:58.645 --> 00:35:01.314
He can't think straight anymore.

239
00:35:05.251 --> 00:35:07.787
I'm not going with you.

240
00:35:09.522 --> 00:35:14.561
Pema, I leave tomorrow at dawn.

241
00:35:26.806 --> 00:35:29.676
Are you ready? Hurry up.

242
00:35:29.676 --> 00:35:32.579
We're ready. Come.

243
00:35:32.579 --> 00:35:37.517
I'm ready too.
- So are we. Let's go.

244
00:36:03.109 --> 00:36:05.278
Karma, your father.

245
00:36:30.003 --> 00:36:33.807
Karma, all our sons
leave together with you.

246
00:36:33.807 --> 00:36:36.476
I didn't force anyone to come with me.

247
00:36:36.476 --> 00:36:39.179
I can't support Tinle.

248
00:36:39.179 --> 00:36:42.649
I wanted you as our leader,
but not like that.

249
00:36:42.649 --> 00:36:44.384
I have no other choice.

250
00:36:44.384 --> 00:36:48.388
If you go sooner
the gods will be against you.

251
00:36:48.388 --> 00:36:53.326
You will be banished from the Dolpo.
- I am taking the Dolpo with me.

252
00:36:53.326 --> 00:36:56.329
You are no longer part of this.

253
00:38:15.308 --> 00:38:17.811
Tinle has returned.

254
00:38:35.528 --> 00:38:38.898
Do you see my son?
- No.

255
00:38:40.133 --> 00:38:42.002
I see Tinle.

256
00:38:43.236 --> 00:38:46.172
Norbou isn't with him.

257
00:38:47.007 --> 00:38:50.777
What's happened?
- Are you alone?

258
00:38:50.777 --> 00:38:56.182
Why? Everyone's here.
- Karma and the others have left.

259
00:38:56.182 --> 00:38:59.119
Where is the salt?
- I've got mine.

260
00:38:59.119 --> 00:39:01.621
Me too.

261
00:39:01.621 --> 00:39:04.791
My sons have all my salt.

262
00:39:04.791 --> 00:39:07.627
What are they doing with our salt?

263
00:39:07.627 --> 00:39:09.930
Same as always.

264
00:39:11.531 --> 00:39:16.603
We're leaving on the set date.
- Tinle, we're too old.

265
00:39:16.603 --> 00:39:20.373
I see a couple of tough and
cooperative men.

266
00:39:21.641 --> 00:39:27.047
Chopga, Paljor, Tensing,
we'll make it together.

267
00:39:27.047 --> 00:39:33.019
Tinle, it's been years.
We can't do this anymore.

268
00:39:33.019 --> 00:39:37.991
The gods are on our side,
the mountains our allies.

269
00:39:37.991 --> 00:39:41.461
In here we will die of embarrassment.

270
00:39:41.461 --> 00:39:46.232
Tinle's right.

271
00:39:50.604 --> 00:39:51.938
Karma.

272
00:39:53.974 --> 00:39:57.911
You did it.
- We did this together.

273
00:39:57.911 --> 00:40:00.280
Long live Karma.

274
00:40:26.139 --> 00:40:29.309
We'll go, just like in the old days...

275
00:40:29.309 --> 00:40:31.845
My old Ngeunpo.

276
00:40:36.516 --> 00:40:40.687
We'll show them.

277
00:40:40.687 --> 00:40:46.493
Father, there is another bag inside.
Do you need it?

278
00:40:46.493 --> 00:40:48.728
Yes, bring it to me.

279
00:41:17.657 --> 00:41:20.760
Pasang, stop that, for Christ's sake.

280
00:41:30.937 --> 00:41:33.440
The salt. Quick.

281
00:41:33.440 --> 00:41:36.443
We must not waste it.

282
00:41:38.011 --> 00:41:40.947
Hurry.

283
00:42:26.393 --> 00:42:28.295
Lama Norbou.

284
00:42:45.378 --> 00:42:48.915
What are you doing here? Go home.

285
00:42:54.054 --> 00:42:57.123
My son is a member of the caravan now.

286
00:43:01.127 --> 00:43:06.433
This one isn't properly attached. It's going to
fall off if you're not careful.

287
00:43:06.433 --> 00:43:08.635
Give me a hand.

288
00:43:11.438 --> 00:43:14.774
Tie a knot in it. Come on.

289
00:43:15.609 --> 00:43:18.878
The blessing will be later.

290
00:43:22.082 --> 00:43:24.384
First we get this knot right.

291
00:43:26.052 --> 00:43:28.555
Is it OK now?
- Yes it'll do.

292
00:43:31.458 --> 00:43:34.794
Put your boots on, boy.

293
00:43:50.243 --> 00:43:53.980
Don't worry.
- Winter is coming.

294
00:43:53.980 --> 00:43:57.550
You are all old men.

295
00:43:57.550 --> 00:44:02.555
What if it's going to snow?
- Don't worry. Pasang will be fine.

296
00:44:02.555 --> 00:44:05.425
We'll take good care of our child.

297
00:44:05.425 --> 00:44:07.928
But you're the child.

298
00:44:48.034 --> 00:44:50.270
Hurry up. Move it.

299
00:45:46.393 --> 00:45:48.528
Come on. Move.

300
00:46:03.810 --> 00:46:05.211
Tinle.

301
00:46:07.047 --> 00:46:11.217
We haven't been here for so long.
- You can say that again.

302
00:46:13.587 --> 00:46:16.156
I'm exhausted.

303
00:46:40.413 --> 00:46:46.253
Are you my father's brother?
- yes. Do I look like you imagined?

304
00:46:46.253 --> 00:46:50.223
Father says you have been
locked up for years.

305
00:46:50.223 --> 00:46:54.361
A monastery is not a prison.
- You weren't locked up?

306
00:46:54.427 --> 00:46:59.566
When you say your prayers
the soul leaves the body.

307
00:46:59.566 --> 00:47:02.335
This is pure freedom.

308
00:47:02.335 --> 00:47:05.205
Where does it leave the body then?

309
00:47:11.278 --> 00:47:14.014
The yaks are gone.

310
00:47:14.014 --> 00:47:17.517
Old Ngeunpo,
run like in the old days.

311
00:47:25.258 --> 00:47:27.327
Go.

312
00:47:35.702 --> 00:47:39.072
Easy, you're scaring them.

313
00:47:39.072 --> 00:47:45.145
Don't wave your arms and legs like that.
- Feel the rhythm of the Yaks.

314
00:47:45.145 --> 00:47:48.081
Don't make any sudden moves.

315
00:47:48.081 --> 00:47:52.986
If you pray to the gods like this
you'll scare them.

316
00:47:56.122 --> 00:47:59.359
Aren't you tired?
- I'm okay.

317
00:48:04.431 --> 00:48:07.701
I've heard you're a good painter.

318
00:48:07.701 --> 00:48:11.004
No, but my frescoes are good.

319
00:48:15.508 --> 00:48:20.914
My father hasn't changed a bit.

320
00:48:20.914 --> 00:48:27.020
When he screams, man and animal bow
their heads and walk past.

321
00:48:27.020 --> 00:48:28.588
But where to?

322
00:48:43.436 --> 00:48:46.273
There they are, back there.

323
00:48:54.281 --> 00:48:57.918
What's happened?
- Suddenly he fell.

324
00:48:57.918 --> 00:49:02.455
The gods are having their revenge.
They're sending evil spirits down.

325
00:49:02.455 --> 00:49:07.827
The gods have left us.
- Karma, what shall we do?

326
00:49:08.695 --> 00:49:11.798
This is your fault.

327
00:49:15.969 --> 00:49:18.738
Here is his poison.

328
00:49:18.738 --> 00:49:21.408
This is our evil spirit.

329
00:49:25.579 --> 00:49:30.083
Whoever's scared tell me,
but don't blame me for it.

330
00:50:20.600 --> 00:50:22.802
Guide the Yaks over here.

331
00:50:50.897 --> 00:50:54.200
Grandfather, my feet hurt.

332
00:50:54.200 --> 00:50:59.839
Do we have to go this far tomorrow??
- Yes, and the days after that too.

333
00:50:59.839 --> 00:51:03.710
Eventually you will
develop  corns under your feet.

334
00:51:03.710 --> 00:51:06.379
You will be a real Dolpopa.

335
00:51:07.747 --> 00:51:11.017
The beginning is tough.
- It stays that way.

336
00:51:11.017 --> 00:51:14.020
Stop whining.

337
00:51:14.020 --> 00:51:17.324
Karma's got a four day lead.

338
00:51:17.324 --> 00:51:20.393
We must overtake them before the pass.

339
00:52:04.671 --> 00:52:08.041
Buddhas of the three era,
Padmasambhava.

340
00:52:08.041 --> 00:52:13.246
Rid us of all obstacles,
internal, external or hidden.

341
00:52:13.246 --> 00:52:15.682
Make our wishes come true.

342
00:52:28.762 --> 00:52:33.867
I'm not walking any further. And I'm hungry.
- Just a little bit.

343
00:52:33.867 --> 00:52:36.169
I'm hungry.

344
00:52:38.271 --> 00:52:41.808
Stop. Everyone.
Pasang is hungry.

345
00:52:41.808 --> 00:52:46.813
Tinle, look, they're tired.
They've stopped.

346
00:52:53.687 --> 00:52:56.222
What's the matter?

347
00:52:58.692 --> 00:53:01.528
I want to go home.

348
00:53:02.662 --> 00:53:06.600
What do we eat
when we don't sell out salt?

349
00:53:06.600 --> 00:53:09.869
Your grandfather has never given up.

350
00:53:13.306 --> 00:53:17.410
Paljor, explain to him...

351
00:53:17.410 --> 00:53:24.017
that a true Dolpopa never gives up.
- I'm too tired for that anyway.

352
00:53:26.086 --> 00:53:29.923
It's because of us you're getting
more and more behind by the day.

353
00:53:29.923 --> 00:53:32.459
Me and Pasang will go back.

354
00:53:32.459 --> 00:53:35.161
No you won't.

355
00:53:35.161 --> 00:53:37.731
What are you going to do in the village?

356
00:53:40.500 --> 00:53:44.671
Pasang belongs here.
- He's still a child.

357
00:53:47.073 --> 00:53:50.243
Yesterday he was one.

358
00:54:34.087 --> 00:54:38.058
Let's sit down.

359
00:54:46.399 --> 00:54:51.738
Tinle said we would stop
by that mountain.

360
00:54:51.738 --> 00:54:53.406
which mountain?

361
00:54:53.406 --> 00:54:58.411
Can you see the shadow on the left side?
There by that mountain ridge.

362
00:54:58.411 --> 00:55:00.614
Next to that ravine?

363
00:55:00.614 --> 00:55:04.351
No, next to that brown mountain.

364
00:55:04.351 --> 00:55:08.021
The one in the sunlight?

365
00:55:08.021 --> 00:55:12.926
What sun?
- What mountain? They're all the same.

366
00:55:35.949 --> 00:55:39.386
You're tired. Lean on me.

367
00:55:39.386 --> 00:55:41.988
I'm younger than you are.

368
00:55:43.256 --> 00:55:45.926
My Yak is getting old.

369
00:55:48.028 --> 00:55:51.364
We've been walking for eight days now.

370
00:55:51.364 --> 00:55:52.832
Eight days?

371
00:56:01.241 --> 00:56:05.345
It's already been ten days since we left.

372
00:57:08.942 --> 00:57:12.579
What's he hoping for?

373
00:57:12.579 --> 00:57:15.849
We'll never gain on Kharma.

374
00:57:15.849 --> 00:57:18.118
He's crazy.

375
00:57:18.118 --> 00:57:22.322
We'll die in here if we're not careful.

376
00:57:22.455 --> 00:57:26.593
We have to end this.
- You tell him.

377
00:57:26.593 --> 00:57:29.996
Me? You're his best friend?

378
00:57:36.469 --> 00:57:39.406
What is that?

379
00:57:39.406 --> 00:57:41.474
A tree.

380
00:57:41.474 --> 00:57:43.810
Will we be seeing trees on our way?

381
00:57:43.810 --> 00:57:45.645
An entire forest.

382
00:57:45.645 --> 00:57:48.582
Have you ever seen a tree?

383
00:57:48.582 --> 00:57:51.084
No.

384
00:57:51.084 --> 00:57:55.822
So how can you draw them?
- My teacher taught me.

385
00:57:58.558 --> 00:58:01.161
how large is a tree?

386
00:58:01.161 --> 00:58:06.499
When you're on top you can see far
, like on a mountain.

387
00:58:06.499 --> 00:58:10.537
Like a leader.
- What do you mean?

388
00:58:10.537 --> 00:58:13.006
Like grandfather.

389
00:58:13.006 --> 00:58:15.675
He can see far.

390
00:58:36.730 --> 00:58:39.032
I'm exhausted.

391
00:58:39.032 --> 00:58:41.101
Wanneer zijn we er?

392
00:58:49.743 --> 00:58:52.178
I'm so tired.

393
00:58:52.178 --> 00:58:53.647
Grandfather.

394
00:59:03.857 --> 00:59:06.126
I'm so tired.

395
00:59:08.228 --> 00:59:12.232
We walk and walk and walk
but we'll never get there in time.

396
00:59:17.504 --> 00:59:20.574
We'll never catch up with Karma.

397
00:59:24.511 --> 00:59:28.348
Be a sensible man.
The boy is exhausted.

398
00:59:29.783 --> 00:59:33.119
If we die it'll be your fault.

399
00:59:36.723 --> 00:59:40.627
We've always helped each other.
We must succeed.

400
00:59:40.627 --> 00:59:43.763
Succeed? At what?

401
00:59:43.763 --> 00:59:47.834
We have no other choice.

402
01:00:03.917 --> 01:00:06.753
Grandfather.

403
01:00:37.784 --> 01:00:44.357
Behind that mountain once leopards
got two of my Yaks.

404
01:00:44.357 --> 01:00:46.660
Ngeunpo's Yaks.

405
01:00:54.868 --> 01:01:01.274
The screaming scares away the leopards.
- Not just the leopards.

406
01:01:01.274 --> 01:01:05.211
The caravan.
It's Karma and the others.

407
01:01:11.551 --> 01:01:15.655
That's not the caravan.
It's the pilgrims.

408
01:01:15.655 --> 01:01:18.058
What are they?

409
01:01:18.058 --> 01:01:21.261
Religious people that walk through mountains.

410
01:01:44.651 --> 01:01:49.522
Where are you from?
- Mount Kailash.

411
01:01:49.522 --> 01:01:54.628
How far is Shey Riwo Dupta?
- Less than ten days from here.

412
01:01:54.628 --> 01:01:58.265
Where are you going?
- To the wheatlands.

413
01:01:58.265 --> 01:02:03.236
Have you seen the caravan?
- Yes, and its two hundred Yaks.

414
01:02:03.236 --> 01:02:06.940
When?

415
01:02:08.275 --> 01:02:12.445
About three, four..
No five days ago.

416
01:02:12.579 --> 01:02:15.081
Can't be more than three days ago.

417
01:02:15.081 --> 01:02:17.584
They were young and
walking at a fast pace.

418
01:02:46.212 --> 01:02:49.149
I thought we could make it.

419
01:02:49.149 --> 01:02:54.554
We can't gain on them.
Karma knows the mountains well.

420
01:02:56.823 --> 01:02:58.858
We'll never make it.

421
01:02:58.858 --> 01:03:04.998
Tinle is too stubborn.
But the mountains have been kind.

422
01:03:04.998 --> 01:03:09.135
In one week we could be
home safely again.

423
01:03:13.573 --> 01:03:17.110
The mountains are our home.
We live for the Yaks and the salt.

424
01:03:17.110 --> 01:03:21.815
It's insane to try
and gain on Karma.

425
01:03:36.229 --> 01:03:41.968
You would be able to finish your fresco.
- That can wait.

426
01:03:41.968 --> 01:03:44.871
Show me your hands.

427
01:03:52.779 --> 01:03:55.548
Why did you come with us?

428
01:03:59.586 --> 01:04:03.223
When you left the monastery...

429
01:04:03.223 --> 01:04:08.795
I remembered the words
of one of my teachers.

430
01:04:08.795 --> 01:04:13.633
'If you have to choose which way to go,
take the most difficult way.'

431
01:04:13.633 --> 01:04:15.602
The most difficult way...

432
01:04:18.805 --> 01:04:21.241
The hardest way.

433
01:04:22.409 --> 01:04:24.578
The hardest way?

434
01:04:48.568 --> 01:04:53.173
Some more tea?
Haven't you had enough yet?

435
01:04:53.173 --> 01:05:00.180
Labrang, don't tell me
you didn't bring any beer.

436
01:05:02.616 --> 01:05:06.786
You've forbidden me to bring beer.
- And you listened to that?

437
01:05:09.456 --> 01:05:12.692
Too bad, we have to
drink Karma's then.

438
01:05:13.793 --> 01:05:16.596
We will take the lake route tomorrow.

439
01:05:17.898 --> 01:05:21.501
For god's sake, Tinle.

440
01:05:21.501 --> 01:05:23.436
The devil's path?

441
01:05:23.436 --> 01:05:27.607
I walked the path long ago once
and I'm still here.

442
01:05:27.607 --> 01:05:32.379
Do evil spirits live there?
- If we make it...

443
01:05:32.379 --> 01:05:36.816
We will be ahead of them by the time we.
reach the pass -You go. I'm leaving

444
01:05:36.816 --> 01:05:40.987
You just go. And keep your frontdoor
locked tightly.

445
01:05:42.389 --> 01:05:46.526
Tinle, you're asking too much of us.

446
01:05:46.526 --> 01:05:49.462
What do you want to eat this winter?

447
01:05:50.397 --> 01:05:52.299
Salt?

448
01:05:53.366 --> 01:05:56.970
I'm going to get our wheat.
We have no other choice.

449
01:05:56.970 --> 01:05:59.906
We will be facing evil spirits.

450
01:06:01.141 --> 01:06:02.609
In the flesh.

451
01:06:08.882 --> 01:06:11.451
Enough praying. We're leaving.

452
01:09:16.169 --> 01:09:18.838
Hold the Yaks.
- What's wrong?

453
01:09:18.838 --> 01:09:21.441
Part of the path fell down.
- Stop.

454
01:09:21.441 --> 01:09:23.777
We can't pass here.

455
01:09:29.282 --> 01:09:35.455
What are you doing?
- The Yaks can't turn around and go back.

456
01:09:35.455 --> 01:09:38.024
We must go through.

457
01:09:38.024 --> 01:09:41.194
Give me that stone.

458
01:09:41.194 --> 01:09:43.964
Not that one. A smaller one.

459
01:09:43.964 --> 01:09:47.000
Where are you going? You're going to fall!

460
01:09:48.134 --> 01:09:50.737
I want to help grandfather.

461
01:09:52.205 --> 01:09:55.408
Be careful.
- Of course I will.

462
01:10:05.552 --> 01:10:09.022
You can't pass. Stay there.

463
01:10:13.260 --> 01:10:14.928
Stop them.

464
01:11:05.812 --> 01:11:08.782
Will this be strong enough?

465
01:11:08.782 --> 01:11:11.051
Are you asking me?

466
01:11:15.055 --> 01:11:17.123
Try it.

467
01:11:30.503 --> 01:11:33.273
Come, Ngeunpo.

468
01:11:33.273 --> 01:11:37.110
If you can make it
all Yaks will.

469
01:11:41.081 --> 01:11:43.149
The path is safe now.

470
01:11:44.284 --> 01:11:47.554
Tundrup built it.

471
01:11:47.554 --> 01:11:50.056
Just like your fence.

472
01:11:52.926 --> 01:11:57.130
Get the Yaks coming one by one.

473
01:12:42.108 --> 01:12:44.244
Oh God.

474
01:12:57.791 --> 01:13:00.860
Careful. There is just enough room.

475
01:13:14.507 --> 01:13:17.611
Step by step.
Give me your hand.

476
01:13:56.216 --> 01:13:58.218
We've made it.

477
01:13:58.218 --> 01:14:03.823
One Yak and two bags of salt.
It is the price the spirits asked.

478
01:14:46.333 --> 01:14:49.569
Look, more pilgrims.

479
01:14:49.569 --> 01:14:52.505
They have Yaks with them.

480
01:14:52.505 --> 01:14:56.276
Are you serious?
- It's a caravan.

481
01:14:57.377 --> 01:15:02.515
It's pilgrims.
- No, it's a caravan.

482
01:15:02.515 --> 01:15:07.387
There is a Lama there.
- It look like that's Ngeunpo.

483
01:15:07.387 --> 01:15:10.257
It's Tinle Yaks.

484
01:15:24.905 --> 01:15:26.973
It's Tinle.

485
01:15:26.973 --> 01:15:31.545
And Pasang, Chopga en Norbou.
They're all there.

486
01:15:31.545 --> 01:15:33.179
Tinle is here.

487
01:15:34.147 --> 01:15:36.516
Karma, Tinle is here.

488
01:16:16.456 --> 01:16:19.092
We'll make camp there.

489
01:16:27.601 --> 01:16:31.771
Welcome Tinle. Join us for a drink.

490
01:16:32.005 --> 01:16:35.809
We'll stay here for two days.
Let us take care of your Yaks.

491
01:16:35.809 --> 01:16:38.044
They're already unloading them.

492
01:16:38.044 --> 01:16:42.983
I didn't know you were this close behind us.
I would've waited.

493
01:16:42.983 --> 01:16:47.921
I haven't been following you.
I left at the date we set.

494
01:16:47.921 --> 01:16:51.458
Bu that's four days after we left.

495
01:16:56.062 --> 01:16:57.864
Four days?

496
01:16:59.165 --> 01:17:02.035
No one can be that fast.

497
01:17:02.035 --> 01:17:06.506
It's impossible
they left so late.

498
01:17:06.506 --> 01:17:09.175
He's done the impossible.

499
01:17:19.619 --> 01:17:24.324
Ling's prophesy. When there's
good weather ahead the salt crackles.

500
01:17:24.324 --> 01:17:29.429
When the weather's going to be bad
it's as silent as the grave.

501
01:17:49.883 --> 01:17:51.985
I don't hear anything.

502
01:17:52.986 --> 01:17:56.556
The salt is silent.
- Bad weather is coming.

503
01:17:56.556 --> 01:17:59.759
We're leaving tomorrow.
- It didn't crackle.

504
01:18:01.294 --> 01:18:03.630
The salt didn't crackle.

505
01:18:09.069 --> 01:18:10.403
Tinle...

506
01:18:12.138 --> 01:18:16.676
we have been walking
for two weeks straight.

507
01:18:18.411 --> 01:18:21.882
Our men and our Yaks are exhausted.

508
01:18:23.083 --> 01:18:25.919
We were going to rest for two days.

509
01:18:25.919 --> 01:18:29.689
The grass is good here and the sky is blue.

510
01:18:31.558 --> 01:18:34.394
The sky is playing games with us.

511
01:18:34.394 --> 01:18:37.731
The salt didn't crackle.

512
01:18:37.731 --> 01:18:40.500
We must cross the pass now.

513
01:18:40.500 --> 01:18:44.604
We can't put our lives at stake
for a handful of salt.

514
01:18:44.604 --> 01:18:49.209
This salt has helped us for centuries.

515
01:18:49.209 --> 01:18:51.912
Are you listening to him?

516
01:18:54.514 --> 01:18:57.017
Salt can't talk.

517
01:18:57.017 --> 01:18:59.586
It's nonsense.

518
01:19:00.687 --> 01:19:03.823
You must take the Gods seriously.

519
01:19:07.627 --> 01:19:12.766
If we survive this
we have ourselves to thank for it.

520
01:19:12.766 --> 01:19:15.902
Ourselves. Not the Gods.

521
01:19:44.464 --> 01:19:46.800
Please understand.

522
01:19:46.800 --> 01:19:50.637
You are a leader,
but not his son.

523
01:19:52.806 --> 01:19:58.011
Sometimes I wonder if Lhakpa...
- He didn't want you to come.

524
01:19:59.179 --> 01:20:02.682
I wanted to follow him.

525
01:20:02.682 --> 01:20:06.152
I should have persisted.

526
01:20:06.152 --> 01:20:08.922
Don't blame yourself for it.

527
01:20:15.161 --> 01:20:17.397
Do you see that star?

528
01:20:18.932 --> 01:20:24.938
If you look closely you'll see
that it beats just like a heart.

529
01:20:26.273 --> 01:20:29.743
It is this star you must learn to find.

530
01:20:29.743 --> 01:20:31.878
There are so many stars.

531
01:20:35.649 --> 01:20:38.285
Yes, but this one star...

532
01:20:40.887 --> 01:20:42.656
is ours.

533
01:20:44.858 --> 01:20:48.795
This is the star that will lead us
to the land of the wheat.

534
01:20:50.230 --> 01:20:56.403
Our grand-grandfathers
already followed this star.

535
01:21:03.510 --> 01:21:05.745
Where is Pasang?

536
01:21:10.383 --> 01:21:13.119
Have you seen Pasang?
- No.

537
01:21:31.238 --> 01:21:34.007
Are you coming with him?

538
01:21:34.007 --> 01:21:39.179
Come with us.
You won't survive the snow storm.

539
01:21:39.179 --> 01:21:41.882
You will die here.

540
01:21:41.882 --> 01:21:45.018
Where is that snow storm?

541
01:21:45.018 --> 01:21:47.621
Have you seen the stars?

542
01:21:47.621 --> 01:21:49.856
Tinle is wrong.

543
01:21:49.856 --> 01:21:52.292
He know these mountains.

544
01:21:52.292 --> 01:21:55.095
Come with us. Do it for me.

545
01:21:55.095 --> 01:21:57.330
You have to choose now.

546
01:21:57.330 --> 01:22:01.134
Either you come with Tinle
or you're staying with me.

547
01:22:01.134 --> 01:22:07.941
You're just like him.
All you ever think of is yourself.

548
01:22:07.941 --> 01:22:12.479
And what about you?
When will you start thinking of yourself?

549
01:22:40.173 --> 01:22:42.976
Karma.

550
01:22:42.976 --> 01:22:44.844
Pasang.

551
01:22:50.317 --> 01:22:52.586
Let him, father.

552
01:22:53.653 --> 01:22:56.022
Stay out of this.

553
01:22:56.022 --> 01:22:58.491
So should you.

554
01:23:03.630 --> 01:23:06.333
Come with us.
- I can't.

555
01:25:40.120 --> 01:25:42.355
Come with us, everyone together.

556
01:25:50.764 --> 01:25:53.033
Help him up.

557
01:26:02.976 --> 01:26:05.278
We're taking the salt.

558
01:26:07.981 --> 01:26:11.384
Tinle's going to get us all killed.

559
01:27:31.031 --> 01:27:33.400
Aren't you cold?

560
01:27:39.940 --> 01:27:44.744
Tinle, let's stop.
We'll never make it across.

561
01:27:44.744 --> 01:27:48.515
We can't even see where the path is.

562
01:27:48.515 --> 01:27:55.188
We must face that storm.
- Let's wait for it to pass.

563
01:27:55.188 --> 01:28:01.761
There is enough food for four days.
If we go back we'll all die.

564
01:28:01.761 --> 01:28:05.932
I am Tinle. Master of the mountains.
- Father...

565
01:28:53.446 --> 01:28:55.849
Are you alright, father?

566
01:28:57.050 --> 01:29:02.122
Don't listen to them. keep going,
even though you're going only slowly.

567
01:29:04.457 --> 01:29:09.196
Do not make camp
before you reach the four Chorten.

568
01:29:09.196 --> 01:29:11.264
Why?

569
01:29:11.264 --> 01:29:15.435
Keep on walking. I'm going to see
if anyone was left behind.

570
01:30:12.158 --> 01:30:14.361
Grandfather.

571
01:30:17.097 --> 01:30:20.300
Straight into the mountains, boy.

572
01:31:14.855 --> 01:31:19.726
Have you seen my father?
- No. I thought he was with you?

573
01:32:44.711 --> 01:32:46.279
Father...

574
01:32:46.279 --> 01:32:48.181
Tinle...

575
01:33:37.364 --> 01:33:41.134
If we're not careful we'll get lost too.

576
01:33:41.134 --> 01:33:46.673
We have to keep searching.
He's got lost in the dark.

577
01:33:46.673 --> 01:33:49.075
There.

578
01:33:50.043 --> 01:33:51.978
Father...

579
01:34:25.545 --> 01:34:29.683
He saw the storm in the clear blue sky.

580
01:34:29.683 --> 01:34:33.854
I didn't see anything.
I walked straight into the trap.

581
01:34:33.854 --> 01:34:38.792
If you'd come with us you
wouldn't have saved him.

582
01:34:41.428 --> 01:34:47.033
Did I save him
or did the mountains spare him?

583
01:36:10.150 --> 01:36:12.752
You don't understand.

584
01:36:12.752 --> 01:36:15.055
He will take everything from you.

585
01:36:15.055 --> 01:36:17.958
You're the leader.

586
01:36:17.958 --> 01:36:21.061
Don't think like that father.

587
01:36:21.061 --> 01:36:23.463
I'm not a leader.

588
01:36:23.463 --> 01:36:28.368
I'm a painter, a son
who helped his father out.

589
01:36:29.436 --> 01:36:31.738
And Pasang?

590
01:36:31.738 --> 01:36:35.909
Pasang has made his decision.
Everything will be alright.

591
01:36:36.009 --> 01:36:38.812
Let them.

592
01:36:56.730 --> 01:37:01.201
Are you going shooting?
- Learn how to saddle your Yak.

593
01:37:08.441 --> 01:37:13.547
Wear this or you will be blinded.

594
01:37:13.547 --> 01:37:17.417
And you'll cry.

595
01:37:22.422 --> 01:37:24.958
The boy is in good hands.

596
01:39:16.036 --> 01:39:18.805
It's up to you now.

597
01:39:23.977 --> 01:39:25.779
Don't forget...

598
01:39:26.713 --> 01:39:30.784
a leader guides his people...

599
01:39:30.784 --> 01:39:34.287
but receives his orders
from the gods.

600
01:39:36.523 --> 01:39:39.092
Don't you ever forget.

601
01:39:43.663 --> 01:39:47.434
I dreamt
that you were my father.

602
01:39:49.836 --> 01:39:52.973
You're too much like me
for me to be your father...

603
01:39:52.973 --> 01:39:55.775
for you to be my son.

604
01:39:58.178 --> 01:40:02.983
Do you think I've never wanted to
defy the Lamas?

605
01:40:04.451 --> 01:40:10.924
A true leader starts by
being disobedient.

606
01:40:28.341 --> 01:40:32.179
The Gods triumph.

607
01:40:57.537 --> 01:41:00.140
What are you doing?

608
01:41:01.374 --> 01:41:05.879
Put me down. I'm staying here.

609
01:41:05.879 --> 01:41:10.884
We will look for herbs to cure you
down in the valley.

610
01:41:10.884 --> 01:41:13.787
You want to cure me?

611
01:41:13.787 --> 01:41:16.857
I'm not ill. I'm old.

612
01:41:16.857 --> 01:41:20.861
Leave him here.
He belongs here, in these mountains.

613
01:41:20.861 --> 01:41:23.263
Chopga's right.

614
01:41:23.263 --> 01:41:25.765
It's what he wants.

615
01:41:27.534 --> 01:41:32.305
Karma, you will have to be their leader.

616
01:41:33.073 --> 01:41:34.941
Just go.

617
01:41:37.744 --> 01:41:40.180
Take good care of Pasang.

618
01:41:41.214 --> 01:41:44.751
You've gotten behind too much
already because of me.

619
01:41:53.126 --> 01:41:55.161
We're almost there.

620
01:41:55.161 --> 01:41:59.332
I can't leave you behind
when I've just found you.

621
01:42:00.800 --> 01:42:03.937
We've always been connected.

622
01:42:03.937 --> 01:42:06.239
We've always wanted the same.

623
01:42:09.776 --> 01:42:11.945
Tinle, please don't die.

624
01:42:14.247 --> 01:42:17.083
Let him go.

625
01:42:17.083 --> 01:42:22.088
He's going to join my father
in Padmasambhava's paradise.

626
01:44:07.994 --> 01:44:10.931
I've learned so much.

627
01:44:11.998 --> 01:44:16.169
From you, my father Tinle,
my brother Lhakpa...

628
01:44:16.203 --> 01:44:21.041
From you, my nephew Pasang
of you, Pema...

629
01:44:21.041 --> 01:44:23.443
and from you, Karma.

630
01:44:23.443 --> 01:44:28.248
This fresco is for you.
It's finished.

631
01:44:28.248 --> 01:44:30.951
It tells a story.

632
01:44:30.951 --> 01:44:33.453
The story of Pasang...

633
01:44:33.453 --> 01:44:37.390
The youth of a leader.

634
01:44:39.492 --> 01:44:41.728
The Gods triumph.
